# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MAREFIYAYE WEB — Environment Configuration Example
# Path: apps/web/.env.example
#
# Purpose:
#   Reference template for environment variables required by the Next.js
#   frontend. Copy to `.env.local` for local dev. In production (Vercel),
#   set these in Project Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# Notes:
#   - `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variables are exposed to the browser at build time.
#     Never put secrets here — they are public.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── API Base URL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev: absolute URL to the Express server.
# Vercel prod: relative "/api/v1" so the Next.js proxy route handles it
#              on the same origin (no CORS, no hardcoded domain).
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000/api/v1